3. INTEGRATED MATHEMATICAL FORMULAS\
The ECU calculates the system state at 100 Hz using these formulas:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Phi = ABS( (V_gps * K_abs) - (Omega_axleB * R_dynamic) )
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i The target value for engagement is Phi < 0.02. V_gps is true vehicle speed, K_abs is the friction coefficient, Omega_axleB is angular velocity, and R_dynamic is the dynamic rolling radius.
\f1\i0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
R_dynamic = R_nominal * (1 - (Load_coeff * Pressure_psi))
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i Accounts for tire deformation based on axle load and tire pressure.
\f1\i0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
T_regen = (0.5 * J * Omega^2) / Delta_t
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i Determines regenerative braking force based on moment of inertia (J), angular velocity (Omega), and time (Delta_t).
\f1\i0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
T_total = T_active(t) + T_standby(t) = Constant
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i Ensures smooth traction during the axle swap sequence.
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
